@startuml option_a_kg_as_mcp_tools
title Option A — KG as MCP tools the LLM can choose

actor User
participant "ask.py\n(CLI)" as CLI
participant "LangGraph\nagent loop" as Agent
participant "LLM\n(Gemini)" as LLM
participant "MCP server\n(FastMCP)" as MCP
participant "Fusion tools\n(search_*, get_buyer)" as FusionTools
participant "KG tools\n(kg_get_entity, kg_get_edge,\nkg_get_pattern, kg_lookup_vocabulary)" as KGTools
participant "FusionClient\n(httpx)" as FusionClient
participant "OracleClient\n(oracledb)" as OracleClient
participant "Oracle 26ai\n(SPIRE schema)" as Oracle
participant "Fusion REST\n(live pod)" as FusionPod

User -> CLI : "Show me suppliers in US\nwith no invoices in 6 months..."
CLI -> Agent : run_agent(prompt)
Agent -> MCP : load_mcp_tools()
MCP --> Agent : Fusion tools + KG tools (combined list)

Agent -> LLM : prompt + tool list + system_prompt
LLM --> Agent : tool_call: kg_get_pattern("country_filter_via_address")
Agent -> MCP : invoke kg_get_pattern
MCP -> KGTools : kg_get_pattern("country_filter_via_address")
KGTools -> OracleClient : SELECT * FROM kg_pattern WHERE pattern_name=...
OracleClient -> Oracle : SQL
Oracle --> OracleClient : row
OracleClient --> KGTools : pattern definition
KGTools --> MCP : pattern details
MCP --> Agent : tool result
Agent -> LLM : updated context

LLM --> Agent : tool_call: kg_lookup_vocabulary("country", "US")
Agent -> MCP : invoke kg_lookup_vocabulary
MCP -> KGTools : kg_lookup_vocabulary(...)
KGTools -> OracleClient : SELECT canonical_value FROM kg_vocabulary...
OracleClient -> Oracle : SQL
Oracle --> OracleClient : "US"
KGTools --> MCP : "US"
MCP --> Agent : "US"
Agent -> LLM : updated context

LLM --> Agent : tool_call: search_suppliers_by_country("US")
Agent -> MCP : invoke search_suppliers_by_country
MCP -> FusionTools : search_suppliers_by_country("US")
FusionTools -> FusionClient : GET /suppliers?expand=addresses
FusionClient -> FusionPod : HTTPS request
FusionPod --> FusionClient : 25 suppliers
FusionClient --> FusionTools : 25 suppliers
FusionTools --> MCP : 25 suppliers
MCP --> Agent : 25 suppliers
Agent -> LLM : updated context

note over LLM, Agent
  Many more iterations:
  kg_get_edge("HAS_INVOICE") to learn join field,
  search_invoices(...) for each candidate,
  kg_get_edge("ASSIGNED_TO") to learn cross-pillar,
  get_buyer(...) per matched PO, etc.
end note

LLM --> Agent : final_answer (no more tool calls)
Agent --> CLI : answer text
CLI --> User : printed answer
@enduml